16 60.16 0 0 1-60.117334 60.074667z m152.917334-275.2A272.64 272.64 0 0 0 591.957333 725.333333h-44.330666v-255.445333a106.666667 106.666667 0 0 0 71.125333-100.096 35.584 35.584 0 1 0-71.125333 0 35.584 35.584 0 0 1-71.082667 0 35.584 35.584 0 1 0-71.125333 0 106.666667 106.666667 0 0 0 71.125333 100.096V725.333333h-47.018667a307.029333 307.029333 0 0 0-87.04-137.984 248.874667 248.874667 0 0 1 169.941334-430.933333 246.101333 246.101333 0 0 1 165.376 63.232 248.661333 248.661333 0 0 1-1.706667 372.693333h-0.085333z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <span data-v-064cc47f="" class="toolcall-title-name-text">Recommend Cloud Only Model for Tara's S10 Skip Local Deployment</span></div> <!----> <div data-v-064cc47f="" class="toolcall-title-container-extra"> <svg data-v-064cc47f="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" aria-hidden="true" role="img" class="iconify toolcall-title-container-extra-arrow" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Right_b"><path d="M681.00096 549.23264a36.864 36.864 0 0 0-0.08192-52.0192L395.22304 211.47648a36.864 36.864 0 1 0-52.14208 52.10112l259.6864 259.72736-259.76832 261.69344a36.864 36.864 0 0 0 52.30592 51.93728l285.696-287.744z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></div></div> <div data-v-897ffb8e="" data-v-8f1d918e="" class="toolcall-content"><div class="scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-top" aria-hidden="true"></div><div data-v-897ffb8e="" class="resize-container" style="height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-897ffb8e="" class="slot-container"><div data-v-8766e0de="" data-v-8f1d918e="" class="markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-8766e0de="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Merlin clarifies: the Termux foreground setup is on his G5. Tara's S10 won't run local models meaningfully better â€” not worth putting a local model on her phone unless she wants to.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Brief reply: agree, skip local on Tara's S10, keep it cloud-only; maybe one nuance â€” the S10 has 8GB vs G5's lower RAM (G5 has 2-4GB depending on variant; Moto G5 has 2-4GB). S10's 8GB would run a small quantized model a bit better, but still not agent-grade. Recommend: Tara's phone runs the native sensor service + maybe Termux for agents occasionally, but the default is the computer runs Hermes/agents, phone is a pure sensor node. That simplifies architecture: if agents live on the computer, Termux on her phone isn't needed at all.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Keep it short. Maybe offer the simplified architecture.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class="scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="scroll-edge-fade-measure-sentinel" aria-hidden="true"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----></div><div data-v-b2cba09c="" class="toolcall-rollup__part toolcall-rollup__flat"><!----> <div data-v-8766e0de="" data-v-e3c80efd="" class="markdown-container"><div data-v-8766e0de="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Agreed â€” and honestly that simplifies Tara's side of the build. If the local-model door is closed on the S10 (and it basically is: 8GB beats the G5's RAM, but a 3B quantized model at a crawl still isn't a <em>coding agent</em>), then there's no reason for Termux to exist on her phone at all.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Which gives you the cleanest possible split:</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Tara's S10</strong> â€” one job. The native sensor service: foreground Kotlin app, opens the magnetometer/IMU/barometer/mic directly, streams over WebSocket, logs to CSV locally as a buffer. No agents, no Termux, nothing to babysit. It boots, it streams, it survives all night because a foreground service with a persistent notification doesn't get killed.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Your G5 (or the computer)</strong> â€” the swarm lives here, since you already know it holds foreground fine.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>The computer</strong> â€” Tara's UI, the MCP server, and optionally Hermes if you want agents co-located with the UI instead of on the G5.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The MCP server then only has one phone to talk to, and it's a dumb, reliable pipe. Less moving parts, fewer 3 AM "why did Termux die" mysteries on a phone that isn't yours to debug.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Only reason to revisit would be if Tara <em>wants</em> a local model for something low-stakes â€” a tiny classifier for "did a knock happen" on-device, say, which doesn't need an LLM at all, just the IMU stream and a threshold. But that's a feature of the sensor app, not a model install.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">So next concrete step stays the same: the Kotlin WebSocket sensor service. Want the protocol sketch â€” message types, rates, the subscribe/poll model for the MCP layer?</div></div></div></div> <div data-v-b2cba09c="" class="toolcall-rollup__tail"><div data-v-b2cba09c="" class="toolcall-rollup__tail-in"><!----></div></div></div> <!----> <!----> <!----></div>  <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!---->   <!----> <div data-v-0754fef1="" class="okc-cards-container"><!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----></div> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <div data-v-ae31b4b4="" data-v-aaf8281b="" class="segment-assistant-actions"><div data-v-ae31b4b4="" class="segment-assistant-actions-content"> <!----> <!----> <!----><div data-v-ab0641ea="" data-v-ae31b4b4="" class="icon-button" style="width: 28px; height: 28px;"><svg data-v-ab0641ea="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333