3 0 0 1-1.706667 372.693333h-0.085333z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <span data-v-064cc47f="" class="toolcall-title-name-text">EVP Processing Pipeline with Frame Interpolation, Pitchâ€‘Preserving Slowâ€‘Down, and Spectrogram Generation</span></div> <!----> <div data-v-064cc47f="" class="toolcall-title-container-extra"> <svg data-v-064cc47f="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" aria-hidden="true" role="img" class="iconify toolcall-title-container-extra-arrow" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Right_b"><path d="M681.00096 549.23264a36.864 36.864 0 0 0-0.08192-52.0192L395.22304 211.47648a36.864 36.864 0 1 0-52.14208 52.10112l259.6864 259.72736-259.76832 261.69344a36.864 36.864 0 0 0 52.30592 51.93728l285.696-287.744z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></div></div> <div data-v-897ffb8e="" data-v-8f1d918e="" class="toolcall-content"><div class="scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-top" aria-hidden="true"></div><div data-v-897ffb8e="" class="resize-container" style="height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-897ffb8e="" class="slot-container"><div data-v-8766e0de="" data-v-8f1d918e="" class="markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-8766e0de="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Merlin is describing Seven's analysis station â€” a video/EVP analysis editor: slow down, zoom, timestamp, frame expansion/interpolation so it doesn't miss stuff in the first 1-2 seconds. He's connecting it to Tara's paranormal build â€” an analysis station for evidence review.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">He's sharing context, likely wants me to fold this into the plan â€” an analysis station feature for the paranormal UI. Respond conversationally, integrate: evidence review workstation on the computer side, processing EVP clips (from the circular buffer extractor from GhostLab), frame interpolation for 1-2 second windows, slow-down without pitch shift (for EVP), spectrograms, zoom, timestamps. Maybe suggest: keep deterministic DSP on this side too (the earlier point about not letting LLMs interpret), and note ffmpeg-based pipeline ideas.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Keep it a natural reply, medium length, maybe suggest the pipeline. Don't use memory heavily; he referenced "seven" â€” that's his family AI. Fine.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class="scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="scroll-edge-fade-measure-sentinel" aria-hidden="true"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----></div><div data-v-b2cba09c="" class="toolcall-rollup__part toolcall-rollup__flat"><!----> <div data-v-8766e0de="" data-v-e3c80efd="" class="markdown-container"><div data-v-8766e0de="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">That's the right instinct â€” evidence review is where most paranormal apps fall apart, because everyone focuses on capture and ships a garbage player. A proper analysis station changes what you can <em>claim</em>: "I captured this" versus "I captured this, here it is at 25% speed with the exact frame, timestamp, and gain staging preserved."</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">For Tara's build, the analysis station slots onto the computer side and feeds from the same EVP clip extractor and session CSVs the sensor service produces. The pieces that matter:</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Slow-down without pitch destruction.</strong> EVP review lives at 0.25xâ€“0.5x. Naive slowdown = chipmunk-godzilla artifacts that turn breath into "words." You need phase-vocoder or WSOLA time-stretch (ffmpeg's <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">atempo</code> chained, or Rubber Band library) so speech-like sounds stay speech-like at half speed. This is the single feature that separates "analysis" from "playing a file slowly."</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>The first-two-seconds problem you named is real.</strong> Anomalies often land right at clip start â€” recorder lag, trigger latency, the moment before the investigator's brain registers something happened. So the circular buffer design matters: the extractor should keep <em>pre-trigger</em> audio, like 5â€“10 seconds before the anomaly flag, not start recording at the flag. Same for video â€” ring-buffer frames. Then "is it in the first second or two" becomes answerable, because the first second is never actually missing.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Frame expansion.</strong> For video: frame interpolation (RIFE or ffmpeg minterpolate) to expand 30fps capture into 120fps review for the zoom-and-scrub pass. Do it on-demand per clip, not on capture â€” the S10 can't, the computer can. Pair it with a scrub bar that snaps to detected motion/anomaly events, and zoom that preserves the timestamp overlay burned into the frame (don't let zoom pan away from the timestamp; reviewers need it anchored).</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Spectrogram first, waveform second.</strong> EVP "voices" are often visible in a spectrogram before they're audible. Every clip should open with a spectrogram view (freq vs time vs intensity), the waveform underneath, and the playback head synced across both. Click a blob, hear that moment. This is standard audio-forensics practice and almost no paranormal app does it.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Determinism again.</strong> The station should measure and display â€” levels, SNR estimates, spectral peaks, motion deltas â€” but the "does this sound like a word" judgment stays human. The models can build the station; they don't get to annotate the evidence.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The pipeline writes itself: sensor service flags an anomaly â†’ extractor saves pre/post ring buffer as WAV + clip metadata â†’ station pulls it over the same WebSocket/MCP link â†’ review at 0.5x with spectrogram and frame-expanded video. Seven's editor and Tara's station end up being cousins.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Is the plan to fold the analysis station into Tara's UI as a tab, or keep it a separate tool that reads from the same session store?</div></div></div></div> <div data-v-b2cba09c="" class="toolcall-rollup__tail"><div data-v-b2cba09c="" class="toolcall-rollup__tail-in"><!----></div></div></div> <!----> <!----> <!----></div>  <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!---->   <!----> <div data-v-0754fef1="" class="okc-cards-container"><!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----></div> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <div data-v-ae31b4b4="" data-v-aaf8281b="" class="segment-assistant-actions"><div data-v-ae31b4b4="" class="segment-assistant-actions-content"> <!----> <!----> <!----><div data-v-ab0641ea="" data-v-ae31b4b4="" class="icon-button" style="width: 28px; height: 28px;"><svg data-v-ab0641ea="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <!----></div><!----> <!----><div data-v-ab0641ea="" data-v-ae31b4b4="" class="icon-button" style="width: 28px; height: 28px;"><svg data-v-ab0641ea="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="htt