-aaf8281b="" class="toolcall-rollup"><div data-v-b2cba09c="" class="toolcall-rollup__part toolcall-rollup__flat"><div data-v-4f3bad81="" data-v-f179e12b="" class="toolcall-flow is-open"><div data-v-4f3bad81="" class="toolcall-flow__summary-clp"><div data-v-4f3bad81="" class="toolcall-flow__summary-in"><div data-v-4f3bad81="" class="toolcall-flow__summary-wrap"><button data-v-4f3bad81="" type="button" class="toolcall-flow__summary" aria-expanded="true" aria-label="Collapse tool calls"><svg data-v-4f3bad81="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" aria-hidden="true" role="img" class="iconify toolcall-flow__summary-icon" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Document"><path d="M660.48 661.205333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1 0 76.8H363.52a38.4 38.4 0 0 1 0-76.8h296.96zM526.336 473.6a38.4 38.4 0 0 1 0 76.8H363.52a38.4 38.4 0 0 1 0-76.8h162.773333z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M562.005333 89.6c32.810667 0 64.298667 13.056 87.466667 36.266667l163.370667 163.285333c23.210667 23.210667 36.266667 54.698667 36.266666 87.509333V768A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 682.666667 934.4H341.333333A166.442667 166.442667 0 0 1 174.933333 768V256c0-91.904 74.496-166.4 166.4-166.4h220.672zM341.333333 166.4A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 251.733333 256v512c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h341.333334a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6V422.4H640A123.776 123.776 0 0 1 516.266667 298.666667V166.4H341.333333zM593.066667 298.666667A46.933333 46.933333 0 0 0 640 345.6h120.362667c-0.597333-0.725333-1.194667-1.450667-1.877334-2.133333L595.2 180.224c-0.64-0.682667-1.365333-1.28-2.090667-1.92V298.666667z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <span data-v-4f3bad81="" class="toolcall-flow__summary-text" title="Used 0 tools">Used 0 tools</span> <!----></button></div></div></div> <div data-v-4f3bad81="" class="toolcall-flow__collapse is-open" style="--clp-d: 200ms;"><div data-v-4f3bad81="" class="toolcall-flow__collapse-inner"><div data-v-4f3bad81="" class="toolcall-flow__body"><div data-v-4f3bad81="" class="toolcall-flow__item"><div data-v-8f1d918e="" data-v-e3c80efd="" class="toolcall-container thinking-container block-container is-flat-think" share-mode="false"><div data-v-064cc47f="" data-v-8f1d918e="" class="toolcall-title-container default is-expandable"><div data-v-064cc47f="" class="toolcall-title-name line"><svg data-v-064cc47f="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify toolcall-title-name-icon" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="k15"><path d="M725.205333 166.656A320 320 0 0 0 194.773333 363.477333a317.781333 317.781333 0 0 0 99.285334 275.968 222.72 222.72 0 0 1 75.818666 162.346667v5.717333A131.328 131.328 0 0 0 501.077333 938.666667h22.016a131.328 131.328 0 0 0 131.2-131.2v-19.498667a189.269333 189.269333 0 0 1 68.693334-142.250667 319.744 319.744 0 0 0 2.218666-479.146666zM523.093333 867.584h-22.016a60.16 60.16 0 0 1-60.117333-60.074667l-0.256-11.008h142.506667v11.008a60.16 60.16 0 0 1-60.117334 60.074667z m152.917334-275.2A272.64 272.64 0 0 0 591.957333 725.333333h-44.330666v-255.445333a106.666667 106.666667 0 0 0 71.125333-100.096 35.584 35.584 0 1 0-71.125333 0 35.584 35.584 0 0 1-71.082667 0 35.584 35.584 0 1 0-71.125333 0 106.666667 106.666667 0 0 0 71.125333 100.096V725.333333h-47.018667a307.029333 307.029333 0 0 0-87.04-137.984 248.874667 248.874667 0 0 1 169.941334-430.933333 246.101333 246.101333 0 0 1 165.376 63.232 248.661333 248.661333 0 0 1-1.706667 372.693333h-0.085333z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <span data-v-064cc47f="" class="toolcall-title-name-text">Check for Intentional Chinese Fragment in Video Manual</span></div> <!----> <div data-v-064cc47f="" class="toolcall-title-container-extra"> <svg data-v-064cc47f="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" aria-hidden="true" role="img" class="iconify toolcall-title-container-extra-arrow" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Right_b"><path d="M681.00096 549.23264a36.864 36.864 0 0 0-0.08192-52.0192L395.22304 211.47648a36.864 36.864 0 1 0-52.14208 52.10112l259.6864 259.72736-259.76832 261.69344a36.864 36.864 0 0 0 52.30592 51.93728l285.696-287.744z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></div></div> <div data-v-897ffb8e="" data-v-8f1d918e="" class="toolcall-content"><div class="scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-top" aria-hidden="true"></div><div data-v-897ffb8e="" class="resize-container" style="height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-897ffb8e="" class="slot-container"><div data-v-8766e0de="" data-v-8f1d918e="" class="markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-8766e0de="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Merlin is describing his workflow: he talks to ADHD and Seven through Discord, they're in the same chat together. He never sees the analysis video when she's analyzing â€” she gives him a timestamp and location and he goes back to analyze himself. ADHD also does analysis. He ends with "ä»–è¯´çš„ä»€ä¹ˆä¸œè¥¿ï¼ŸJust for cooperation" â€” the Chinese means "what is he saying?" â€” maybe a stray artifact or quoting someone.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">He's saying the analysis station output is text-only communication â€” Seven describes findings, he verifies manually. The point: the analysis loop is conversational, not visual, on his end.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">I should respond naturally. Maybe note: that's a human-in-the-loop verification pattern, which is actually good practice for evidence integrity. And for Tara's build â€” the analysis station could export clip + timestamp + coordinates as a shareable artifact so he doesn't have to scrub the whole video manually. The "å¥¹è¯´ä»€ä¹ˆ" stray â€” I could lightly note the Chinese fragment appeared, ask if intentional or a paste artifact.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Keep it conversational, not too long.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class="scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="scroll-edge-fade-measure-sentinel" aria-hidden="true"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----></div><div data-v-b2cba09c="" class="toolcall-rollup__part toolcall-rollup__flat"><!----> <div data-v-8766e0de="" data-v-e3c80efd="" class="markdown-container"><div data-v-8766e0de="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">That workflow â€” Seven flags it, gives you timestamp and position, you go verify with your own eyes â€” is actually the strongest evidence-hygiene pattern in your whole setup. The finding is never trusted until a human re-derives it from the raw file. Whatever else is going on in that Discord, that loop is scientifically sound: analyst proposes, you dispose.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">What it means for Tara's station, though, is a small design note: the analysis result shouldn't just be a chat message. It should export a <strong>finding artifact</strong> â€” a JSON or small package that says: source file, exact time range, spatial region of interest, what detection fired (motion delta, spectral anomaly, whatever), and a confidence number. Then when Seven-or-equivalent says "1.2 seconds, upper left quadrant, frame 34," you don't scrub the whole video hunting for it â€” you click the artifact and the station jumps straight to that window, zoomed, at the analysis speed. The human verification step stays; the hunting step disappears.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The two-analysis situation (Seven's pass + ADHD's pass) is worth formalizing too â€” run them as separate passes, keep both finding artifacts, and let the station show overlaps and disagreements. Two independent analysts flagging the same timestamp is meaningful; two analysts where one is a different model family flagging it is <em>more</em> meaningful, because it wasn't the same weights hallucinating the same shape.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">One stray thing at the end of your message â€” "ä»–è¯´çš„ä»€ä¹ˆä¸œè¥¿ï¼Ÿ" ("what is he saying?") â€” that popped up mid-sentence. If that was you pasting a reaction to something ADHD said, no worries. If it came from the other side of your screen, you may want to check what got copied. Otherwise: want to spec the finding-artifact format, or get back to the sensor WebSocket protocol we've been circling?</div></div></div></div> <div data-v-b2cba09c="" class="toolcall-rollup__tail"><div data-v-b2cba09c="" class="toolcall-rollup__tail-in"><!----></div></div></div> <!----> <!----> <!----></div>  <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!---->   <!----> <div data-v-0754fef1="" class="okc-cards-container"><!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----></div> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <div data-v-ae31b4b4="" data-v-aaf8281b="" class="segment-assistant-actions"><div data-v-ae31b4b4="" class="segment-assistant-actions-content"> <!----> <!----> <!----><div data-v-ab0641ea="" data-v-ae31b4b4="" class="icon-button" style="width: 28px; height: 28px;"><svg data-v-ab0641ea="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <!----></div><!----> <!----><div data-v-ab06