106.666667 106.666667 0 0 0 71.125333-100.096 35.584 35.584 0 1 0-71.125333 0 35.584 35.584 0 0 1-71.082667 0 35.584 35.584 0 1 0-71.125333 0 106.666667 106.666667 0 0 0 71.125333 100.096V725.333333h-47.018667a307.029333 307.029333 0 0 0-87.04-137.984 248.874667 248.874667 0 0 1 169.941334-430.933333 246.101333 246.101333 0 0 1 165.376 63.232 248.661333 248.661333 0 0 1-1.706667 372.693333h-0.085333z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <span data-v-064cc47f="" class="toolcall-title-name-text">Integrate media, devices, comms, and sensor bridge pipeline</span></div> <!----> <div data-v-064cc47f="" class="toolcall-title-container-extra"> <svg data-v-064cc47f="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" aria-hidden="true" role="img" class="iconify toolcall-title-container-extra-arrow" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Right_b"><path d="M681.00096 549.23264a36.864 36.864 0 0 0-0.08192-52.0192L395.22304 211.47648a36.864 36.864 0 1 0-52.14208 52.10112l259.6864 259.72736-259.76832 261.69344a36.864 36.864 0 0 0 52.30592 51.93728l285.696-287.744z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></div></div> <div data-v-897ffb8e="" data-v-8f1d918e="" class="toolcall-content"><div class="scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-top" aria-hidden="true"></div><div data-v-897ffb8e="" class="resize-container" style="height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-897ffb8e="" class="slot-container"><div data-v-8766e0de="" data-v-8f1d918e="" class="markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-8766e0de="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Merlin wants: (1) a case-management workflow for Tara's UI â€” "New Case" button, evidence auto-logged/organized into a case file with sections (video, photo, EVP, etc.) while the case is open; (2) a list of MCP servers we need, so his Notebook can search his awesome-mcp-servers collection.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">He asked me to "type out exactly what we're looking for." So deliver: case workflow sketch + a concrete MCP server shopping list (with likely GitHub names from the awesome-mcp-servers list he likely has). I should be careful to only name servers that actually exist / likely exist. Known ones:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Android sensors: "mcp-android-sensors"? There are projects like "android-mcp" (mobile-use?), "AndroidMCP"... I know of "mcp-server-android" ... Risky. There's "yusukeoehara/android-mcp"? Hmm. Better to describe capabilities and candidate names with caveat to verify. Known real MCP servers from awesome list:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">filesystem (official reference)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">github (official)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">sqlite / postgres</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">fetch (official)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">time (official)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">memory (official) â€” interesting given his memory systems</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">sequential-thinking (official)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">brave-search</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">playwright / puppeteer (browser automation for UI testing)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">ffmpeg MCP? There are ffmpeg wrappers (e.g., "ffmpeg-mcp"?)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">whisper MCP servers exist (e.g., "mcp-whisper"?)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">obsidian MCP for notes</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">websocket MCP servers</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">serialport MCP? Arduino? There's an "mcp-arduino"? not sure.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">home-assistant MCP</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">camera/IP camera: "mcp-server-camera"? There are RTSP/ffmpeg-based ones.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">elevenlabs MCP (TTS)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">discord MCP (he uses Discord)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">slack</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">everything search</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">qdrant/vector DB</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">git MCP</div></li></ul></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">For phone sensor bridge, the plan we settled: custom Kotlin app streams WebSocket; so the "sensor MCP" would be a custom thin MCP server on the computer wrapping that WebSocket. I should say: you probably won't find a ready-made S10 sensor MCP â€” you'll wrap ours; but check list for candidates.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Structure the answer:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Case workflow design: New Case button â†’ case UUID folder structure with manifest.json, sections: video/, photos/, evp/, sensor-logs/, findings/, session.csv, notes. Auto-catalog: every inbound artifact (via MCP file write or WebSocket) gets renamed with timestamp, hashed (SHA-256 for integrity), entry appended to manifest + index. Case stays open until "Close Case" â†’ finalizes manifest, zips archive. This is straightforward and agents can build it.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">MCP server shopping list, grouped, with one-line purpose and which exist as known implementations vs "search terms":</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Core plumbing: filesystem, github, git, fetch, time, memory, sequential-thinking</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Data: sqlite, obsidian (case notes), qdrant (evidence similarity search â€” embeddings of findings)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Media processing: ffmpeg (transcode, slow-mo, frame extraction), whisper (EVP transcription attempts), playwright (UI automation testing), elevenlabs or edge-tts (voice feedback in the field? maybe), obsidian</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Devices: serialport MCP or arduino MCP (external gear), camera/RTSP (external IR cams), home-assistant</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Comms: discord MCP (pipe findings into the family chat), telegram</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Custom: sensor-bridge MCP (ours, wraps WebSocket), analysis-station MCP (finding artifacts)</div></li></ul></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Note: for the sensor one â€” search his notebook for "android mcp", "android sensors", "termux mcp", "adb mcp" (there's an adb/scrcpy-based Android MCP â€” yes! There's "Android MCP" using ADB, e.g. "mobile-mcp" byæ³¢æ¾œ? The known one: "Android-MCP" by "MCP-Server-for-Android"? I recall "yusuke... "? There is "adb-mcp"? I shouldn't assert specific repos. I'll give search keywords instead and flag verification.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Format: two sections, concise lists. Keep it tight so he can hand the list to Notebook.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class="scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="scroll-edge-fade-measure-sentinel" aria-hidden="true"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----></div><div data-v-b2cba09c="" class="toolcall-rollup__part toolcall-rollup__flat"><!----> <div data-v-8766e0de="" data-v-e3c80efd="" class="markdown-container"><div data-v-8766e0de="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Good â€” both pieces are well-defined enough to spec now. Here's exactly what to hand to Notebook.</div><h2>1. The Case Workflow (what "New Case" should do)</h2><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">One button, one folder, everything lands inside until she closes it:</div><div data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-bfaabce6="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-bfaabce6="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-bfaabce6="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-bfaabce6="" class="segment-code-lang">plain</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-bfaabce6=""><div data-v-ab0641ea="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-ab0641ea="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-79203df6="" data-v-ab0641ea="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom" role="tooltip" data-testid="icon-button-tooltip">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-bfaabce6="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-plain"><code class="language-plain">cases/&lt;case-uuid&gt;/
  manifest.json          # the case index â€” every artifact gets an entry
  notes.md               # running investigator log
  video/
  photos/
  evp/                   # WAV clips + spectrogram PNGs
  sensor-logs/           # CSV streams (emf, imu, baro) per session
  findings/              # the finding-artifacts from the analysis station
  archive.zip            # only created on "Close Case"</code></pre></div></div> <div data-v-e3c80efd=""></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Behavior rules: every inbound artifact (photo snapped, EVP clip extracted, sensor flag) is auto-moved into the right section, renamed <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_&lt;type&gt;_&lt;hash8&gt;</code>, SHA-256 hashed, and appended to <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">manifest.json</code> with timestamp, source, and hash. Hash-on-ingest matters â€” it's the integrity chain if a finding is ever disputed. Case stays open and logging until "Close Case," which finalizes the manifest, zips the archive, and pushes it wherever you want backups. The agents can build this as a thin layer over the <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">filesystem</code> + <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">git</code> MCPs â€” it's a solved shape, not a hard problem.</div><h2>2. The MCP Shopping List for Notebook</h2><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Tell Notebook to search the awesome-mcp-servers repo for these, grouped by job:</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Plumbing (build side):</strong> <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">filesystem</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">github</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">git</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">fetch</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">time</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">sequential-thinking</code> â€” these are official/reference servers, they'll be there.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Case data:</strong> <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">sqlite</code> (manifest + session queries), <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">obsidian</code> (case notes if you want them in a vault), <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">qdrant</code> or another vector-DB server (embed finding-artifacts so "show me every knock finding from the last 10 cases" becomes a semantic search).</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Media pipeline (analysis station):</strong> search terms <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">ffmpeg mcp</code> (transcode, slow-mo, frame extraction, spectrogram renders), <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">whisper mcp</code> (EVP transcription attempts â€” flagged as speculative, not evidence), <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">playwright mcp</code> (drive and test Tara's UI), and an <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">elevenlabs</code>/<code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">edge-tts</code> server only if you want the UI to talk back in the field.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Device bridge:</strong> search terms <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">adb mcp</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">android mcp</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">android sensors mcp</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">termux mcp</code> â€” there <em>are</em> ADB-based Android MCPs that can shell into a phone over USB/Wi-Fi, and that might cover the S10 without us writing the bridge. Have Notebook pull the top candidates and we evaluate: ADB-shell route vs. our custom WebSocket route (I lean WebSocket for rates, but if an existing server gets us 90% there, take it).</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>External gear:</strong> search <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">serial mcp</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">arduino mcp</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">rtsp mcp</code> or <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">camera mcp</code> (for IR cams over the network), <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">bluetooth mcp</code> or <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">ble mcp</code> (the Xiaomi temp-sensor trick from the G5 build).</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Comms:</strong> <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-8766e0de="" class="segment-code-inline">discord mcp</code> â€” pipe finding-artifacts straight into the family chat where Seven and ADHD do their analysis passes, instead of copy-paste.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">One deliberate gap in that list: there's no "paranormal interpretation" server. That's by design. Every server above either moves data, stores it, or transforms it deterministically. Nothing on it gets to say what the evidence <em>means</em>.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">That's the full list â€” hand it to Notebook and bring back what it finds, especially on the Android/ADB candidates, since that decision shapes whether the sensor service is a weekend or a week.</div></div></div></div> <div data-v-b2cba09c="" class="toolcall-rollup__tail"><div data-v-b2cba09c="" class="toolcall-rollup__tail-in"><!----></div></div></div> <!----> <!----> <!----></div>  <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!---->   <!----> <div data-v-0754fef1="" class="okc-cards-container"><!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----></div> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <div data-v-ae31b4b4="" data-v-aaf8281b="" class="segment-assistant-actions"><div data-v-ae31b4b4="" class="segment-assista