7752="" data-v-e3c80efd="" class="user-content"><!----> <span data-v-a7697752="" class="user-content__text">### **1. Case Workflow Review (`cases/&lt;case-uuid&gt;/`)**

The proposed case directory structure is a **forensic-grade specification**. Storing raw evidence in immutable subdirectories, renaming files deterministically (`YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_&lt;type&gt;_&lt;hash8&gt;`), calculating **SHA-256 hashes on ingest**, and appending every entry to `manifest.json` provides an undeniable chain of custody. 

Because this architecture relies on deterministic filesystem operations and manifest updates, agents can implement this as a thin orchestration wrapper using standard **`filesystem`** and **`git`** MCP servers without needing custom database infrastructure.

---

### **2. MCP Shopping List Search Results**

The notebook directories indexed across `awesome-mcp-servers` sources include the following candidates for your stack:

#### **Plumbing (Build Side)**
* **`filesystem`**: **`@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem`** (official reference server), **`fast-filesystem-mcp`** (large file handling and streaming), and **`mark3labs/mcp-filesystem-server`** [i, ii, iii].
* **`github`**: **`github/github-mcp-server`** (official GitHub integration for repos, issues, and PRs) [i].
* **`git`**: **`@modelcontextprotocol/server-git`** (official reference server for git logs, diffs, and commits) [i].
* **`fetch`**: **`@modelcontextprotocol/server-fetch`** (official reference server) and **`zcaceres/fetch-mcp`** [i, ii].
* **`time`**: **`@modelcontextprotocol/server-time`** (official reference server) [i].
* **`sequential-thinking`**: **`@modelcontextprotocol/server-sequential-thinking`** (official reference server for multi-step reasoning) [i].

#### **Case Data &amp; Memory**
* **`sqlite`**: **`jparkerweb/mcp-sqlite`**, **`run-sql-connectorx`**, and embedded SQLite RAG servers like **`haiku.rag`** [i, ii].
* **`obsidian`**: **`MarkusPfundstein/mcp-obsidian`** (via Obsidian Local REST API), **`bitbonsai/mcpvault`**, and **`jacksteamdev/obsidian-mcp-tools`** [i, ii, iii].
* **`qdrant` / Vector DBs**: **`qdrant/mcp-server-qdrant`** (official Qdrant memory server), **`chroma-mcp`**, and **`mcp-server-milvus`** [i, ii, iii].

#### **Media Pipeline (Analysis Station)**
* **`ffmpeg mcp`**: **`video-creator/ffmpeg-mcp`** (runs local FFmpeg CLI commands for transcoding, audio extractions, and frame renders) [i]. Supplemented by **`Probe.dev`** for forensic metadata extraction with FFprobe and MediaInfo [i].
* **`whisper mcp` / Speech-to-Text**: **`Audioscrape`** (remote MCP server for semantic audio search and timestamped transcripts) [i] and **`mbailey/voicemode`** (voice interaction and speech-to-text) [i].
* **`playwright mcp`**: **`microsoft/playwright-mcp`** (official Playwright browser automation) and **`executeautomation/mcp-playwright`** [i, ii].
* **`elevenlabs` / TTS**: **`elevenlabs/elevenlabs-mcp`** (official ElevenLabs voice synthesis server) and **`mberg/kokoro-tts-mcp`** (local open-weight TTS) [i, ii].

#### **External Gear &amp; Comms**
* **External Gear / Hardware**: **`stack-chan/stack-chan`** and **`horw/esp-mcp`** (ESP32 / hardware control), **`Coreflux MQTT`** (IoT messaging broker), and **`tevonsb/homeassistant-mcp`** (Home Assistant smart device control) [i, ii, iii].
* **`discord mcp`**: **`SaseQ/discord-mcp`** (Java/Spring Boot MCP server for Discord message dispatch and channel reading) [i].

---

### **3. Android / ADB Device Bridge Candidates**

The directory catalogs contain several ADB-based Android MCP servers:

1. **`hao-cyber/Phone Control (Android ADB)`** (`Phone Control`): Remotely manages Android phones over ADB to make calls, send texts, launch apps, manage contacts, and pull device files [i].
2. **`Android MCP`**: Provides ADB control for screenshot capture, UI layout inspection, package management, and raw ADB command execution [i].
3. **`hyperb1iss/droidmind`**: Controls Android devices via ADB for debugging, system analysis, and UI automation [i].
4. **`mobile-next/mobile-mcp`**: Cross-platform Android/iOS device automation server [i].

#### **Evaluation: ADB MCP Route vs. Custom WebSocket Route**

| Dimension | ADB MCP Route (`hao-cyber/Phone Control`, `Android MCP`) | Custom WebSocket Route |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Setup Effort** | **Zero code required** â€” plug in via USB/Wi-Fi and start issuing tools [i]. | Requires building a custom Android app/service on the phone. |
| **File / Media Transfer** | **Excellent** â€” pulling photos (`photos/`) and video clips (`video/`) directly via shell commands [i]. | Moderate â€” requires custom HTTP/socket file upload endpoints. |
| **Sensor Streaming (EMF, Baro, IMU)** | **Poor** â€” polling `dumpsys` or shelling into `getevent` over ADB caps sample rates and introduces latency. | **Superior** â€” Streams raw sensor samples at high frequency (20â€“100Hz) straight into CSV files (`sensor-logs/`). |

**Recommendation**: Use a **hybrid approach**. Leverage an existing ADB MCP server (**`Android MCP`** or **`droidmind`**) for out-of-the-box phone lifecycle management, UI triggers, screenshotting, and media file ingestion, while routing high-frequency sensor CSV logging over a simple, dedicated WebSocket server on the phone [i, ii].

